  "scheme": "dark_red",
  "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
  "voice_script": "She was called the next Steve Jobs, a visionary who would revolutionize healthcare. Elizabeth Holmes promised hundreds of medical tests from a single drop of blood. With this promise, she raised nearly a billion dollars, valuing her company, Theranos, at $9 billion. But behind the curtain, the miracle technology was a complete fiction. The blood tests were secretly being run on commercial machines made by her competitors. It was one of the biggest frauds in modern history, endangering patients and duping the world's most powerful investors. After a landmark trial, the Silicon Valley prodigy's fall was complete.",
